            "text": "Engaging the core is essential for maintaining proper alignment and preventing injury in yoga poses.",
            "event": "ADD"
        },
        {
            "id": "1",
            "text": "To ensure core engagement, focus on keeping the spine neutral and engaging the muscles between the ribs and pelvis.",
            "event": "ADD"
        },
        {
            "id": "2",
            "text": "In Hanumanasana (monkey pose), engage the core to maintain control and balance, especially when the knee is bent.",
            "event": "ADD"
        },
        {
            "id": "3",
            "text": "In Gomukhasana (cow face pose), engage the core to maintain control and balance, especially when the knee is bent.",
            "event": "ADD"
        },
        {
            "id": "4",
            "text": "Use a strap or towel to deepen the stretch or maintain proper alignment, if needed.",
            "event": "ADD"
        }
    ]
}

